{"id": 16, "ts": 1780595160.404456, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s initial support for Candidate\u202fD, especially his strong responsibility, problem\u2011solving, and concentration. However, the new evidence that Candidate\u202fC \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d and \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d directly addresses two of our most safety\u2011critical criteria\u2014stress resilience and decision quality. Moreover, C is noted as 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, which speaks to operational reliability and crew cooperation.\nWhile C does have concerns\u2014difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric style, and limited willingness to pursue further education\u2014these issues are, in my view, more manageable through targeted training and coaching than the unresolved question of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s ability to accept feedback or adapt to criticism. Both D\u2019s arrogance and weak leadership raise red flags for crew dynamics, and we have no concrete observations showing he can mitigate those tendencies.\nGiven the concrete proof of C\u2019s calmness under pressure and rapid, correct decision\u2011making, I would now recommend Candidate\u202fC for the long\u2011distance pilot role, provided we address his communication and development gaps during onboarding."}
